{\f1\fs40 Juniper 2.4 launch notes}\par
{\f1\fs30 What ships}\par
{Juniper 2.4 brings shared invoices, a weekly summary email, and a faster export. Every workspace gets it on October 14.}\par
{\f1\fs30 Shared invoices}\par
{An invoice can now be shared with a link. The client sees the same totals you do, and can pay from the page.}\par
{Discounts and tax are worked out on the server, so the numbers on a shared invoice always match the ones in your books.}\par
{\f1\fs30 Export}\par
{Notwithstanding the aforementioned deprecation of the legacy export pathway, customers whose workspaces were provisioned prior to the migration cutoff will continue to retain read-only access to historical archives until such time as the retention window, which is itself subject to the plan-tier-dependent policy described in Appendix C, has elapsed.}\par
{The new export writes CSV and PDF, and takes about a tenth of the time.}\par
{\f1\fs30 Weekly summary}\par
{Anyone can turn on a Monday or Friday email that lists last week's invoices, payments and overdue accounts.}\par
{\f1\fs30 Known issues}\par
{Tax on discounted invoices is being checked; a fix is in review.}\par
{Very large exports may still time out on the Starter plan.}\par
{\f1\fs30 Rollout}\par
{Staff workspaces get 2.4 first, then ten percent of customers, then everyone over three days.}\par
